{
  "id": 6,
  "title": "Overlaps and underlaps versus defensive state",
  "definition": "off_ball_run events with subtype overlap or underlap. Success is measured by three outcomes already on the run or joined to it: lead_to_shot, xthreat, and beaten_by_movement. A run fails a binary outcome when that outcome is false. xthreat stays continuous. Defensive state is measured from tracking at the midpoint frame of the run, not from the hypothesis-5 tracked flag. Nearest defender distance is the distance to the nearest outfield opponent. Goal-side means that opponent is closer to the goal being attacked than the runner is. The lane is occupied when any outfield opponent is within 1.5 m of the segment from the ball carrier to the runner, with segment parameter t in [0.10, 0.90]. The 6 m split is only a distance band for the xthreat contrast. It is not a tracking rule and it is not a prevention system. beaten_by_movement comes from an on_ball_engagement whose targeted player is the runner and whose frame window meets the run within 1.0 s. Runs with no such engagement are left missing on that outcome.",
  "population": "overlap and underlap off_ball_run",
